{"causes": ["The inherent fragmentation of Tibetan political power contributed to persistent regional conflicts and the rise of competing noble lineages.", "The Tsangpa dynasty, initially vassals, grew increasingly strong, challenging the Rinpungpa's suzerainty through strategic alliances and military expansion.", "Internal strife and a weakening of central authority within the Rinpungpa domain diminished their ability to resist external pressures effectively."], "effects": ["The Rinpungpa dynasty lost its political and territorial control in Central Tibet, marking the end of its significant regional influence.", "The Tsangpa dynasty consolidated power across Tsang, establishing a new dominant force in Central Tibetan politics.", "The political vacuum and subsequent power shifts contributed to the complex religious and political alignments that led to the rise of the Dalai Lamas."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "tsangpa-dynasty", "targetName": "Tsangpa Dynasty", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa's reign and fall occurred during the period of the Tsangpa dynasty's rise to power in Central Tibet."}, {"sourceSlug": "karma-tseten", "sourceName": "Karma Tseten", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "targetName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "context": "Karma Tseten's military campaigns directly led to the overthrow and dispossession of Ngawang Jigme Drakpa in 1565."}, {"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "history-of-the-rinpungpa", "targetName": "History of the Rinpungpa", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa authored the 'History of the Rinpungpa' (Rin spungs pa'i rgyal rabs), a primary historical account of his own dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "tsang-tibet", "targetName": "Tsang, Tibet", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa served as the last ruling prince of the Rinpungpa dynasty, which controlled the region of Tsang in Central Tibet."}, {"sourceSlug": "rinpungpa-dynasty", "sourceName": "Rinpungpa Dynasty", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "phagmodrupa-dynasty", "targetName": "Phagmodrupa Dynasty", "context": "The Rinpungpa dynasty, to which Ngawang Jigme Drakpa belonged, had previously succeeded the direct rule of the Phagmodrupa dynasty in much of Central Tibet."}], "places": [{"name": "Rinpung, Tibet", "role": "Dynastic Seat"}, {"name": "Shigatse, Tibet", "role": "Major Tsangpa Center"}, {"name": "Central Tibet", "role": "Region of Influence"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2382671", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ngawang_Jigme_Drakpa"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa's demise as the last Rinpungpa ruler marked the definitive end of a century-long dynastic power in Central Tibet, directly enabling the rise of the Tsangpa regime which dominated the region for the next 60 years. His personal historical writings also provide crucial primary source material for understanding 16th-century Tibetan political and cultural life.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-23T18:45:40Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45235672042", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa was the last ruling prince of Tsang of the Rinpungpa Dynasty. He was also a renowned author. His increasingly chaotic reign ended in 1565, when the Tsangpa dynasty deprived the Rinpungpa of their main possessions.", "newValue": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa (Ngag dbang 'jigs med grags pa) was the final ruling prince of Tsang from the Rinpungpa dynasty, whose reign marked the twilight of a significant regional power in Central Tibet during the mid-16th century. Born into a lineage that had dominated much of Tsang (western Central Tibet) since the late 15th century, he inherited a fragile state increasingly beset by internal dissent and the burgeoning power of rival factions. His rule, which effectively concluded in 1565, represents a pivotal moment in Tibetan political history, transitioning from the Rinpungpa's Sakya-aligned influence to the ascendancy of the Tsangpa dynasty, who were staunch patrons of the Karma Kagyu school.

Drakpa's period of governance was characterized by escalating instability, a stark contrast to the Rinpungpa's earlier dominance. The dynasty, once a formidable force, found its authority eroded by the ambitions of its former vassals, particularly the Tsangpa regime led by Karma Tseten. In 1565, Karma Tseten's forces decisively defeated the Rinpungpa, seizing their principal strongholds, including Rinpung itself, and effectively dismantling their territorial control. This military defeat stripped Ngawang Jigme Drakpa of his temporal power, although he lived until 1597, dedicating his later years to scholarly pursuits.

Beyond his political role, Ngawang Jigme Drakpa was a distinguished scholar and author, contributing significantly to Tibetan literature and historiography. His most notable work, the 'History of the Rinpungpa' (Rin spungs pa'i rgyal rabs), provides invaluable insights into his dynasty's rise and fall, offering a unique perspective from a participant observer. The collapse of the Rinpungpa under his leadership paved the way for the Tsangpa's consolidation of power across Central Tibet, a precursor to the eventual establishment of the Ganden Phodrang government under the Dalai Lamas with Mongol backing in the 17th century."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T18:45:40Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45235672042", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1482"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "1482"}], "newValue": ["The inherent fragmentation of Tibetan political power contributed to persistent regional conflicts and the rise of competing noble lineages.", "The Tsangpa dynasty, initially vassals, grew increasingly strong, challenging the Rinpungpa's suzerainty through strategic alliances and military expansion.", "Internal strife and a weakening of central authority within the Rinpungpa domain diminished their ability to resist external pressures effectively."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T18:45:40Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45235672042", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "1597"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1597"}], "newValue": ["The Rinpungpa dynasty lost its political and territorial control in Central Tibet, marking the end of its significant regional influence.", "The Tsangpa dynasty consolidated power across Tsang, establishing a new dominant force in Central Tibetan politics.", "The political vacuum and subsequent power shifts contributed to the complex religious and political alignments that led to the rise of the Dalai Lamas."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T18:45:40Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45235672042", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "RULES", "targetSlug": "field-221", "targetName": "Monarchs & Rulers", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa: Sovereign authority in monarchs & rulers"}, {"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "medieval", "targetName": "Medieval Era", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa was active during the Medieval era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "tsangpa-dynasty", "targetName": "Tsangpa Dynasty", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa's reign and fall occurred during the period of the Tsangpa dynasty's rise to power in Central Tibet."}, {"sourceSlug": "karma-tseten", "sourceName": "Karma Tseten", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "targetName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "context": "Karma Tseten's military campaigns directly led to the overthrow and dispossession of Ngawang Jigme Drakpa in 1565."}, {"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "history-of-the-rinpungpa", "targetName": "History of the Rinpungpa", "context": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa authored the 'History of the Rinpungpa' (Rin spungs pa'i rgyal rabs), a primary historical account of his own dynasty."}, {"sourceSlug": "ngawang-jigme-drakpa", "sourceName": "Ngawang Jigme Drakpa", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "tsang-tibet", "targetName": "Tsang, Tib